<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy son of Mennaeus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 40 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy son of Mennaeus was the ruler of the Ituraeans in the 1st century BCE, with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> in the Beqaa valley. He extended his power towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and the coast during the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> confirmed him in power in 63 BCE in return for a large payment. He was succeeded by his son Lysanias.</p></div>
